  "reply_text": "Found one merge-blocking issue in `sms-segments` against `main`:\n\n**[P1] `fits_one_segment` counts characters instead of UTF-8 bytes** — `sms/segment.py:5`\n`len(text)` undercounts non-ASCII messages, violating the documented 160-byte limit. For example:\n- `'é' * 81` is **162 bytes**, but returns `True`.\n- `'😀' * 41` is **164 bytes**, but returns `True`.\n\nBoth correctly return **2** from `segment_count`, so the two APIs disagree about whether these messages fit in one text. Use the existing `utf8_len` helper for this check, and add multibyte boundary tests (80/81 accented characters and 40/41 emoji).\n\nAll 4 existing tests pass, but the fit-check tests cover only ASCII. No files changed.",
